  "response": "To specify which registry URI to use for JFrog or MLflow with `promptfoo scan-model`, you'll need to provide the appropriate URI format in your command. Here's how you can do it based on the context provided:\n\n### For MLflow Registry\n\n- Use the `models:/` URI format.\n- Example command:\n  ```bash\n  promptfoo scan-model models:/MyModel/1\n  ```\n\n### For JFrog Artifactory\n\n- Use the full URL of the model stored in your JFrog Artifactory instance.\n- Example command:\n  ```bash\n  promptfoo scan-model \"https://your-domain.jfrog.io/artifactory/models/model.pkl\"\n  ```\n\n### Authentication\n\nBefore scanning, ensure you have set the necessary environment variables for authentication:\n\n- **MLflow Authentication**:\n  ```bash\n  export MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=\"https://your-mlflow-server.com\"\n  export MLFLOW_TRACKING_USERNAME=\"your-username\"\n  export MLFLOW_TRACKING_PASSWORD=\"your-password\"\n  ```\n\n- **JFrog Artifactory Authentication**:\n  ```bash\n  export JFROG_URL=\"https://your-domain.jfrog.io\"\n  export JFROG_API_TOKEN=\"your-api-token\"\n  ```\n\nThese commands and configurations should help you specify and authenticate the registry URIs for scanning models with `promptfoo scan-model`.",
